  "description": "These strange, bottom-dwelling fish—that resemble a cross between a sting ray and a fish—are really sharks with pectoral fins so large they're referred to as \"wings.\" This is more apparent if you take home one of its two \"wings\" without having your fishmonger do anything (like skinning or filleting it).",
